rlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}}]}}
{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Task: an orphaned attestation must publish the entries it hid\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository, which is in /workspace (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Background:** the ledger writer attests ranges of entries with a predicate `{\"from_seq\", \"to_seq\", \"prev_sha256\", \"head_sha256\"}`. If a run attests a range and then fails, an \"orphan\" record explains that attestation. A reviewer found that an orphan explained only by its statement could hide an attested entry, such as a failing verdict.\n\n**Required:** add a function to `record/record.py`:\n\n    _orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None\n\n- `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes (as produced by `R.canonical(entry)`).\n- Return `None` when the decoded entries are exactly the attested range: there are `to_seq - from_seq + 1` of them, the first chains from `pred[\"prev_sha256\"]` (its `prev` field), each next one chains from the previous one's sha256, and the sha256 of the last one's canonical bytes equals `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`.\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\n  - one containing the word `range` when the count is wrong;\n  - one containing `chain` when an entry's `prev` doesn't link;\n  - one containing `head` when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`.\n- Wire it into wherever orphans are checked, so an orphan without valid hidden entries is reported.\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`."}],"timestamp":1794512784293}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Task: an orphaned attestation must publish the entries it hid\n\nYou are working in `record/` of this repository, which is in /workspace (`record/record.py` and its tests in `record/test_record.py`).\n\n**Background:** the ledger writer attests ranges of entries with a predicate `{\"from_seq\", \"to_seq\", \"prev_sha256\", \"head_sha256\"}`. If a run attests a range and then fails, an \"orphan\" record explains that attestation. A reviewer found that an orphan explained only by its statement could hide an attested entry, such as a failing verdict.\n\n**Required:** add a function to `record/record.py`:\n\n    _orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None\n\n- `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes (as produced by `R.canonical(entry)`).\n- Return `None` when the decoded entries are exactly the attested range: there are `to_seq - from_seq + 1` of them, the first chains from `pred[\"prev_sha256\"]` (its `prev` field), each next one chains from the previous one's sha256, and the sha256 of the last one's canonical bytes equals `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`.\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\n  - one containing the word `range` when the count is wrong;\n  - one containing `chain` when an entry's `prev` doesn't link;\n  - one containing `head` when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`.\n- Wire it into wherever orphans are checked, so an orphan without valid hidden entries is reported.\n- All existing tests in `record/test_record.py` must still pass.\n\nRun the tests with `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record`."}],"timestamp":1794512784293}}
