als `pred[\"head_sha256\"]`.\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\n  - one containing the word `range` when the count is wrong;\n  - one containing `chain` when an entry's `prev` doesn't link;\n  - one containing `head` when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`.\n\nMy implementation seems to match this. Let me verify by writing a quick test script to ensure the function works as expected.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"All existing tests pass. Now let me verify the implementation by writing a quick test to ensure the new function works correctly. Let me also check if there are any edge cases I might have missed.\\n\\nActually, let me also think about the `_orphan_entries_problem` function more carefully. The task says:\\n- `orphan[\\\"body\\\"][\\\"entries_b64\\\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes (as produced by `R.canonical(entry)`).\\n- Return `None` when the decoded entries are exactly the attested range: there are `to_seq - from_seq + 1` of them, the first chains from `pred[\\\"prev_sha256\\\"]` (its `prev` field), each next one chains from the previous one's sha256, and the sha256 of the last one's canonical bytes equals `pred[\\\"head_sha256\\\"]`.\\n- Otherwise return a short problem string:\\n  - one containing the word `range` when the count is wrong;\\n  - one containing `chain` when an entry's `prev` doesn't link;\\n  - one containing `head` when the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`.\\n\\nMy implementation seems to match this. Let me verify by writing a quick test script to ensure the function works as expected.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"All existing tests pass. Let me verify the new function works correctly with a quick test:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-85ae7953-8f6a-4877-a940-7fee3d1d7f21","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport record as R\nimport base64\nimport hashlib\n\n# Create a simple chain with two entries\nchain = []\ne1 = {'seq': 1, 'prev': None, 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': 'test', 'test': 'test', 'decision_rule': 'test'}}\nraw1 = R.canonical(e1)\nh1 = hashlib.sha256(raw1).hexdigest()\nchain.append((e1, h1))\n\ne2 = {'seq': 2, 'prev': h1, 'kind': 'verdict', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test2', 'plan': {'seq': 1, 'sha256': h1}, 'outcome': 'pass', 'evidence': []}}\nraw2 = R.canonical(e2)\nh2 = hashlib.sha256(raw2).hexdigest()\nchain.append((e2, h2))\n\n# Test predicate for range 1-2\npred = R.range_predicate(chain, 1, 2)\nprint('Predicate:', pred)\n\n# Test orphan with correct entries\norphan_correct = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode(), base64.b64encode(raw2).decode()]}}\nprint('Correct orphan:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_correct, pred))\n\n# Test orphan with wrong count\norphan_wrong_count = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode()]}}\nprint('Wrong count:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_wrong_count, pred))\n\n# Test orphan with broken chain\norphan_broken_chain = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode(), base64.b64encode(raw2).decode()]}}\n# Modify the second entry's prev\nimport json\ne2_modified = json.loads(raw2.decode())\ne2_modified['prev'] = '0' * 64\nraw2_modified = R.canonical(e2_modified)\norphan_broken_chain = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode(), base64.b64encode(raw2_modified).decode()]}}\nprint('Broken chain:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_broken_chain, pred))\n\n# Test orphan with wrong head\norphan_wrong_head = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(raw1).decode(), base64.b64encode(raw2).decode()]}}\npred_wrong_head = dict(pred, head_sha256='0' * 64)\nprint('Wrong head:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan_wrong_head, pred_wrong_head))\n\nprint('All tests passed!')\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a5